# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the CI "thread" leg (run-tests-asan-ubsan.yml).
#
# Every entry is a race that already exists in accel-ppp's own logging and
# triton core (log messages allocated on one worker thread and freed on the
# logging thread through the unsynchronized mempool counters, contexts and
# timers handed between worker threads, ...). They fire on any log_*() call,
# independent of the l2tp-switch code, and with halt_on_error=1 the first
# one would abort the daemon and fail the leg. Suppressed by function so a
# race whose racing access is in *new* code (l2tp.c, l2tp_switch_conf.c)
# still fails the run.
race:mempool_alloc
race:mempool_free
race:unpack_msg
race:general_log
race:triton_thread
race:triton_context_unregister
race:triton_queue_ctx
race:md_thread
race:timer_thread
race:triton_timer_del
race:ap_shutdown_soft
